      "dom_id": "question-60624",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14199152/assets/435f50f68f1d5d206a935ec9b00dcd53e7a68647875e21f36d70379e3915a4c5.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the height and base of the triangle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =12 \\\\ \\text{height} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 12\\times 12 \\\\  & =6\\times 12 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in inches, the area is measured in square inches. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=72\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\n$$",
