      "dom_id": "question-93149",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Claire has sectioned off a triangular area of her garden whose base is $7$ feet and height is $5$ feet to plant some flowers. What is the area of the flowerbed?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the flowerbed based on the description.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14199152/assets/b409d299208280d3be7e33be8e74c3d894fa9f3ad7e5605e4b551b6b0434302a.png)\n\nThe height and base of the triangle are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =7, \\\\ \\text{height} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 7\\times 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 35 \\\\  & =17.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in feet, the area is measured in square feet. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=17.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\n$$",
